    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d792">

                <pb facs="1263" n="1249" xml:id="pg1249"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">740.00116 E.W./9–1644: Telegram</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The Consul at Algiers</hi> (<hi
                            rendition="#italic">Lawton</hi>)<anchor n="34"
                        xml:id="d792-f1"/>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">to the Secretary of State
                    </hi>
                </head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Algiers</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1944-09-16T18:00:00+02:00">September 16,
                            1944—6 p.m.</date>
                        <lb/> [Received 11:58 p.m.]</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>67. Note dated September 5 sent to Massigli incorporated Department’s 2554 [<hi
                        rendition="#italic">2555</hi>] September 2, 8 p.m. Acknowledgment received
                    today from Foreign Affairs Commissariat concludes with final paragraph
                    summarized as follows: “Provisional Government” being established in Paris,
                    Commissariat can only reserve comment on whether issuance of new declaration
                    would not be useful in present circumstance. Idea of following and intensifying
                    propaganda already made of subject responds exactly to suggestion expressed by
                    French authorities. Commissariat would be grateful to have competent services
                    requested to renew and develop as frequently as possible in its German language
                    broadcasts warnings already given regarding atrocities committed against
                    civilians, prisoners and internees.</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Lawton</hi>
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
    <standOff>
        <listAnnotation>
            <note corresp="#d792-f1" n="34" type="source" xml:id="d792-f1-content">
                <p>Edward P. Lawton had been relieved of his duties as secretary to the Mission at
                    Algiers on September 13, the Mission having moved on to Paris.</p>
            </note>
        </listAnnotation>
    </standOff>
